# --- PREDICTION for F15. Not a measurement; basis in F15-prep.md task 4. ----------------------------------------------
# Assumes the freeze commit is 542f540b or a later commit that changes only infra/, docs/, .github/ and scripts/check-self-contained.sh. Dev at 5bd4c97c fits (id commit, #35, #36). Recheck with git diff --name-only at the cut.
# RECHECK 2026-11-03: that assumption no longer holds. main c0bafb78 also changes supervisor code (#39: sessionrepo, sessionlaunch, workflow; dev adds cmd/tbound and corpus/sampling).
#   The predictions below still stand: every changed input feeds a value already predicted to CHANGE; base-images.lock.json is unchanged; 20-r1 default mode still reuses the pair. See F15-prep.md, Recheck 2026-11-03.
# BUNDLE_DIGEST: predicted to CHANGE. adapter/src/broker-provider.ts, proxy-tools.ts and ipc-transport.ts changed since 02f9fb71, and all three are P2 extension sources (scripts/prepare_official_pi_runtime.py EXTENSION_FILES).
# IMGDIGEST: predicted to CHANGE. adapter/src is layered into the image (packaging/governed/cell_image.py:243-248), and the image epoch is the freeze commit time (30-p3.sh:14).
# ENTRYPOINT_DIGEST: predicted to CHANGE, inferred and not built. The cell entrypoint imports piruntime in non-test files, and piruntime's non-test files changed.
# CAL_RO_DIGEST and CAL_RW_DIGEST: predicted UNCHANGED. The default 20-r1 mode reuses and re-verifies the installed F14 pair (20-r1.sh:4-9).
# Follow-on, inferred: CFG changes with IMGDIGEST (epoch), BASE_TD changes because it embeds expected_image_digest (guest-10-upgrade.sh.txt:158),
#   LOAD_TAR_DIGEST changes with the image, SRC_DIGEST changes because the archive includes infra/ and corpus/ (20-p1.sh:19),
#   and TBOUND_DIGEST and TBP_DIGEST change because supervisor non-test code changed.
# BASH_DIGEST and NODE_DIGEST: predicted UNCHANGED (base image pins come from packaging/governed/base-images.lock.json, unchanged since 02f9fb71).
# TBP_DIGEST changing is what makes 05-runtime-swap.sh need the (02f9fb71, F15) measurer pair. Without it, the pre-swap check fails at 05:91, before any guest write (05:116).
